        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "b3051edb-bf03-52cd-9008-cc05ae3f0512",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: 41st Tactical Squadron, German Luftwaffe, Mikoyan design bureau\n- Products: Mikoyan MiG-29, Sukhoi Su-27, McDonnell Douglas F-15 Eagle, General Dynamics F-16 Fighting Falcon\n- Concepts: air superiority fighter\n- Places: Soviet Union\n\nFacts:\n- During the 1970s, the Mikoyan design bureau developed the Mikoyan MiG-29 as an air superiority fighter.\n- During the 1970s, the Mikoyan design bureau developed the Mikoyan MiG-29 alongside the larger Sukhoi Su-27 to counter the American McDonnell Douglas F-15 Eagle and General Dynamics F-16 Fighting Falcon.\n- The Mikoyan MiG-29 is a twin-engine jet fighter aircraft designed in the Soviet Union.\n- The Mikoyan MiG-29 has the NATO reporting name Fulcrum.\n- The 41st Tactical Squadron operates Mikoyan MiG-29 jet fighters acquired from the German Luftwaffe.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
